  "avoidBefore": "lower",
  "energy": "Mostly aerobic: races run at an average of about 87-93% of max heart rate for 20 min to 2 h or more, with short anaerobic surges in sprints and transitions and an eccentric leg load on the descents.",
  "summary": "Ski mountaineering is a high-volume uphill endurance sport with a downhill that hammers the knees and thighs. The plan uses heavy, low-rep single-leg and hinge strength to make climbing cheaper and descents safer, with calf, hip and back work, while most of the fitness comes from climbing.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "claim": "Elite male ski mountaineers averaged a VO2max of 71 ml/kg/min against 62.5 in sub-elite; individual races average 93% of max heart rate and even downhills about 85%.",
      "source": "Bortolan et al. 2021, Frontiers in Physiology",
      "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2021.737249/full",
      "grade": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "claim": "In a survey of 104 ski mountaineers, most injuries were in the lower body and the knee was the most common site (29.6%); injured skiers did fewer core sessions and more ski sessions a week.",
      "source": "Etayo-Urtasun et al. 2022, Sports",
      "url": "https://doaj.org/article/ea312ccea325459a9d04f6a10e2dd758",
      "grade": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Heavy strength training added to endurance training improves running and cycling economy and performance.",
      "source": "Ronnestad & Mujika 2014, Scandinavian Journal of Medicine and Science in Sports",
      "url": "https://www.inigomujika.com/en/2013/08/13/optimizing-strength-training-for-running-and-cycling-endurance-performance-a-review-2/3040/",
      "grade": "strong"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "limited",
